# Typography components

Always prefer the shared typography components over raw `<h1>`–`<h6>`, `<p>`, or ad-hoc Tailwind text classes when rendering UI copy.

Components live in `apps/web/src/core/shared/components/ui/`:

| Component | Use for |
|-----------|---------|
| `Display` | Hero/marketing headlines (`level`: d1, d2, d3) |
| `Heading` | Page and section titles (`level`: h1–h6; use `as` for semantic tag) |
| `Paragraph` | Body copy, descriptions, captions (`size`: p1–p6; `tone`: primary–quaternary) |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<h1 className="text-2xl font-semibold">{title}</h1>
<p className="text-muted-foreground mt-1">{description}</p>

// ✅ GOOD
<Heading level="h3" as="h1">{title}</Heading>
<Paragraph className="mt-1">{description}</Paragraph>
```

Exceptions (keep raw elements or utility classes):

- Form labels → `Label` / `FormLabel`
- shadcn primitives that already wrap typography (`CardTitle`, `CardDescription`, etc.)
- Markdown or rich-text renderers
- When no typography variant fits and a one-off utility is intentional in design-system docs
